N1  - <p>Project description chapter in a distributed/grid computing book. Two project papers point to it as the detailed description of Proteins@Home: BMC Bioinformatics 2008 says "Proteins@Home is discribed in more detail elsewhere [49]" (Results), and Proteins 2009 says "The Proteins@Home platform and project will be described in detail elsewhere" (ref. 71). The project's archived website publishes the same material as "The inverse protein folding problem: structure prediction and protein design with Proteins@Home" (Simonson, Mignon, Schmidt am Busch, Lopes, Bathelt, Madigou), including a section titled "Protein design on the BOINC distributed computing platform" (http://web.archive.org/web/20090926232911/http://biology.polytechnique.fr/proteinsathome/documentation2.php). Publisher is cited as Tektum Publishers (Berlin) in the project's papers; the book itself was produced by Rechenkraft.net e.V.</p>
